 ## Overview
-Spatially Constrained Optimization is a post-processing constraint workflow applied to differentiable bitmap or Gaussian primitives to enforce full opacity rendering of target objects and clean up boundary artifacts [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem where applying an opacity loss alone forces primitives to render fully opaque but leaves low-opacity "ghost" primitives lingering on object boundaries, which degrade visual quality [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from standard pruning strategies by re-initializing transparent primitives rather than removing them, thereby maintaining primitive count and coverage in complex regions [S1, unofficial].
+Spatially Constrained Optimization is a post-processing constraint workflow applied to differentiable bitmap or Gaussian primitives to enforce full opacity rendering of target objects and clean up boundary artifacts [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem where applying an opacity loss alone forces primitives to render fully opaque but leaves low-opacity "ghost" primitives lingering on object boundaries, which degrade visual quality [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from standard pruning strategies by re-initializing transparent primitives rather than removing them, thereby maintaining primitive count and coverage in complex regions [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Pruning and Opacity Management](9314-pruning-and-opacity-management.md) and differs from siblings such as [GES Optimization Strategy](4697-ges-optimization-strategy.md), [Temporal Sensitivity Pruning](6350-temporal-sensitivity-pruning.md), [Opacity Split for Cloning](9694-opacity-split-for-cloning.md), [GRay Optimization Settings](10037-gray-optimization-settings.md), and [Opacity Reset & Densification Trigger](10759-opacity-reset-densification-trigger.md).
 
